Orbital tests when the gate acts on constituents: effective Gaussian gate v*_eff = sqrt(v*^2+2s^2),
amplitude (1+2s^2/v*^2)^(-3/2).  Sun: ion thermal dispersion s_sun (assumed 100-300 km/s, interior
temperatures ~1e6-1e7 K); Earth-Moon: s = 1.1 km/s (assumed).
  v* =     0.1: Mars-precession bound |eps| < 6.97e-02 / 2.13e+00 / 1.61e+01 (s_sun 100/200/300); LLR |eps| < 1.85e-07 (v*_eff = 1.56 km/s)
  v* =     1.0: Mars-precession bound |eps| < 6.97e-05 / 2.13e-03 / 1.61e-02 (s_sun 100/200/300); LLR |eps| < 3.15e-10 (v*_eff = 1.85 km/s)
  v* =    10.0: Mars-precession bound |eps| < 7.06e-08 / 2.14e-06 / 1.61e-05 (s_sun 100/200/300); LLR |eps| < 8.01e-10 (v*_eff = 10.12 km/s)
  v* =   120.0: Mars-precession bound |eps| < 1.53e-10 / 1.86e-09 / 1.13e-08 (s_sun 100/200/300); LLR |eps| < 1.06e-07 (v*_eff = 120.01 km/s)
  v* =  1000.0: Mars-precession bound |eps| < 1.22e-09 / 1.41e-09 / 1.76e-09 (s_sun 100/200/300); LLR |eps| < 7.39e-06 (v*_eff = 1000.00 km/s)

